WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:03.541
- All right everybody, welcome
to the "Kelly Clarkson Show."

00:00:03.541 --> 00:00:04.480
Give it up for My Band Y'all,
and their incredible dancers.

00:00:06.489 --> 00:00:10.197
(audience applauding)
(Kelly clapping)

00:00:10.197 --> 00:00:13.960
That was "She Used to be Mine"
from Waitress The Musical.

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.560
I've always loved that song,

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.190
but there's actually a special reason

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:18.170
that I sing it today.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:19.130
Check out this tweet,

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:21.190
it's the sweetest thing from the account

00:00:21.190 --> 00:00:22.960
of Waitress The Musical.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.610
They wrote requesting that
I sing it before the end

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:26.980
of their Broadway run.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.530
Sara Bareilles, who I love,
who is an original cast member

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:33.240
even retweeted it, so I
couldn't pass up the invite.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.130
So we have actually, the actress
that's currently starring

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.900
is Jenna and Waitress joining us.

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:41.264
So let's say hi to Sierra Renée y'all.

00:00:41.264 --> 00:00:42.961
(Audience applauding)

00:00:42.961 --> 00:00:47.961
- [Kelly] Hi, oh my gosh!
We're so happy to have you.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.540
- I'm so happy to be here. Thank you.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.610
- Well, I'm so honored that
y'all wanted me to sing.

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.040
First of all, that song, I love that song.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.470
It's so beautiful, by the way.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.040
God, so empowering to sing,

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.920
feels like, I've gotta raw
moment every time you sing it.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.920
But what's it been like, coming
back to play this character?

00:01:05.121 --> 00:01:07.540
- It's been wild and
strange and beautiful.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.300
I obviously like everyone
else in the theater community,

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:13.790
so missed performing and
telling these beautiful stories.

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:15.500
But to be able to step into this story

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.780
which is just so wonderful and so humane,

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.560
and of course with this
incredible music by Sara Bareilles

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.380
and this script by Jessie
Nelson, it's a dream come true.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:28.330
- Oh my gosh. Well you have
a few shows left, right?

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:31.890
- Yes, we have two more
days and four more shows.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:34.500
So grab your tickets and come on.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.110
- Oh my gosh you must be having

00:01:36.110 --> 00:01:38.900
this feeling of like bitters sweet,

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:40.160
'cause you love doing it,

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.170
but at the same time, you're
like it's that finish line

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:43.003
that's kind of cool too.

00:01:43.003 --> 00:01:44.690
Are you kind of both feelings right now?

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:49.160
- Yeah, absolutely that,
it's always sad to say bye

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.740
to any show, especially
one that's so meaningful

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:54.520
and powerful as this one
and also like so fun.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.190
- Yeah
- And so much

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:59.472
of a family that we've
built together, the cast,

00:01:59.472 --> 00:02:02.288
but yeah, always moving on to
the next thing as an actor.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.340
(audience applauding)

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:05.507
- Thank you for being on the show.

00:02:05.507 --> 00:02:07.087
(Kelly clapping)
(kelly laughing)

